WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.600
Aim a narrow beam of light
at a calm water surface,

2
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:05.840
at 60 degrees to the normal.

3
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:09.860
As it enters the water, the
beam suddenly changes direction.

4
00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:13.000
Now aim it straight
down, along the normal.

5
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:16.470
This time it goes straight
on, with no bend at all.

6
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.700
Same light, same water.

7
00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.950
Why does it bend at an
angle, but not head-on?

8
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.850
In this mission, you'll
picture light as wavefronts,

9
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.300
with rays at right angles to them.

10
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:32.080
Then you'll use Snell's law to
predict exactly how far a ray bends.

11
00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:35.800
Your mission: explain why
light bends as it enters water,

12
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.030
but not when it arrives head-on.
